SPU thread-local state of lifted code, through exported accessors (SPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS).

With SPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS the lifted SPU code reaches g_spu_trampoline_fn, g_spu_pch and g_spu_pch_n through functions
the host exports (spu_tramp_slot, spu_pch_arr, spu_pch_n_slot) instead of naming the host's thread-local variables.
A module built as its own loadable image needs that where the linker rejects a TLS reference into another image (PE).
On macOS the module binds to the host's TLS when it is loaded, so for Resistance 3 the accessors are the base of
module-abi/0002, which caches the trampoline slot in the context: the launcher's module build (launcher/r3_launcher/module.py) builds the SPU lift with
SPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS (without it every SPU trampoline store went through _tlv_get_addr, 1.0-1.5% of the SPU threads'
time in a firefight, against 0.35-0.43% with 0002; 2026-10-26). Without the macro the headers are unchanged.

The PPU accessor (ppu_tramp_slot, PPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS in the PPU lifter's prologue) and the SPURS job's
SPURS_JOB_TLS -> SPU_THREAD_LOCAL respelling (the two macros expand the same) were dropped in the move to v0.19.0: the
port builds the PPU lift against the host's thread-locals directly since d0ae79a, and nothing in it defines
PPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS.

Test: tools/test_spu_module_tramp_slot.py (module-abi/0002) builds a "module" unit with SPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS and checks
the accessor path.

Upstream: not proposed.
---

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_context.h b/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
index 400b2ba5..19de9422 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
@@ -893,2 +893,13 @@ void spu_indirect_branch(spu_context* ctx);
 
+#ifdef SPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS
+/* Lifted images built as a separate loadable module (dll/dylib/so) reach the thread-local variables
+ * below through one accessor per variable that the host exports (spu_drain.c): a PE linker rejects a
+ * TLS reference to a symbol in another image, and the trampoline slot is cached in the context (below). */
+void (**spu_tramp_slot(void))(spu_context*);
+uint32_t (*spu_pch_arr(void))[8];
+unsigned *spu_pch_n_slot(void);
+#  define g_spu_trampoline_fn (*spu_tramp_slot())
+#  define g_spu_pch           (*spu_pch_arr())
+#  define g_spu_pch_n         (*spu_pch_n_slot())
+#else
 /* Pending cross-function transfer target; NULL when none. Thread-local: each
@@ -902,2 +913,3 @@ extern SPU_THREAD_LOCAL uint32_t g_spu_pch[8];
 extern SPU_THREAD_LOCAL unsigned g_spu_pch_n;
+#endif
 
diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c b/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c
index 49bc2b94..b041f62c 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_drain.c
@@ -34,2 +34,7 @@ SPU_THREAD_LOCAL unsigned g_spu_pch_n;
 
+/* Accessors for lifted images built as a separate module (see SPU_MODULE_ACCESSORS in spu_context.h). */
+void (**spu_tramp_slot(void))(spu_context*) { return &g_spu_trampoline_fn; }
+uint32_t (*spu_pch_arr(void))[8] { return &g_spu_pch; }
+unsigned *spu_pch_n_slot(void) { return &g_spu_pch_n; }
+
 /* yz_lockstep_tick now has its real body in spu_lockstep.c (milestone 2). */
